            <ArticleTitle>Cardiac magnetic resonance imaging illustrating Anderson-Fabry disease progression.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>e249-51</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1259/bjr/52065763</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Anderson-Fabry disease is an X-linked lysosomal storage disorder resulting from a deficiency of the enzyme α-galactosidase A (α-Gal A) and subsequent cellular storage of the enzyme's substrate globotriaosylceramide (Gb3) and related glycosphingolipids. We report a case of Anderson-Fabry disease with cardiac involvement evaluated with cardiovascular MRI. Disease progression was observed despite enzyme replacement therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
